- name: epy_block_1
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "import numpy as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\nimport struct\nimport\
      \ zlib\nimport time\nimport os\nimport inspect\n\n# Synchronous PRBS whitening\
      \ keystream matching transmitter\n_rng = np.random.RandomState(42)\nWHITENING_KEY\
      \ = _rng.randint(0, 256, size=2048, dtype=np.uint8)\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n\
      \    \"\"\"Robust QPSK File Deframer, CRC32 Verifier & In-Window GUI Progress\
      \ Display\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, save_dir=\".\"):\n        gr.sync_block.__init__(\n\
      \            self,\n            name='File Deframer & GUI',\n            in_sig=[np.uint8],\n\
      \            out_sig=[]\n        )\n        self.save_dir = str(save_dir)\n\
      \        \n        # 32-symbol preamble matching transmitter\n        self.preamble\
      \ = np.array([3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 3, 0, 3, 3, 3, 3,\n            \
      \                      3, 3, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 3, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 3, 0, 3], dtype=np.uint8)\n\
      \        \n        self.buffer = np.array([], dtype=np.uint8)\n        \n  \
      \      # Transfer state\n        self.current_file_id = None\n        self.file_name\
      \ = \"\"\n        self.file_size = 0\n        self.expected_crc = 0\n      \
      \  self.total_chunks = 0\n        self.received_chunks = {}\n        self.is_completed\
      \ = False\n        self.saved_file_path = \"\"\n        \n        # Statistics\n\
      \        self.total_packets = 0\n        self.crc_errors = 0\n        self.last_preview_text\
      \ = \"\"\n        \n        # GUI Injection\n        self.top_block = None\n\
      \        self.status_label = None\n        self.progress_bar = None\n      \
      \  self.result_label = None\n        self.text_preview = None\n        self.gui_timer\
      \ = None\n        \n        for frame_info in inspect.stack():\n           \
      \ frame = frame_info.frame\n            if 'self' in frame.f_locals:\n     \
      \           val = frame.f_locals['self']\n                if hasattr(val, 'top_grid_layout'):\n\
      \                    self.top_block = val\n                    break\n     \
      \               \n        if self.top_block:\n            try:\n           \
      \     from PyQt5.QtWidgets import QLabel, QTextEdit, QVBoxLayout, QWidget, QProgressBar\n\
      \                from PyQt5.QtCore import QTimer\n                \n       \
      \         self.gui_container = QWidget()\n                layout = QVBoxLayout(self.gui_container)\n\
      \                layout.setContentsMargins(4, 4, 4, 4)\n                layout.setSpacing(4)\n\
      \                \n                self.status_label = QLabel(\"Waiting for\
      \ QPSK File Signal... [Packets: 0 | CRC Errors: 0]\")\n                self.status_label.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                    \"background-color: #1e1e2e; color: #a6e3a1; font-size:\
      \ 14px; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px; border-radius: 4px;\"\n           \
      \     )\n                layout.addWidget(self.status_label)\n             \
      \   \n                self.progress_bar = QProgressBar()\n                self.progress_bar.setRange(0,\
      \ 100)\n                self.progress_bar.setValue(0)\n                self.progress_bar.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                    \"QProgressBar { background-color: #313244; color: #ffffff;\
      \ border-radius: 4px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; height: 22px; }\
      \ \"\n                    \"QProgressBar::chunk { background-color: #89b4fa;\
      \ border-radius: 4px; }\"\n                )\n                layout.addWidget(self.progress_bar)\n\
      \                \n                self.result_label = QLabel(\"Status: Idle\"\
      )\n                self.result_label.setStyleSheet(\n                    \"\
      background-color: #181825; color: #f9e2af; font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;\
      \ padding: 4px; border-radius: 4px;\"\n                )\n                layout.addWidget(self.result_label)\n\
      \                \n                self.text_preview = QTextEdit()\n       \
      \         self.text_preview.setReadOnly(True)\n                self.text_preview.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                    \"background-color: #11111b; color: #cdd6f4; font-family:\
      \ 'Consolas', monospace; font-size: 12px; border: 1px solid #313244; border-radius:\
      \ 4px;\"\n                )\n                self.text_preview.setMinimumHeight(180)\n\
      \                layout.addWidget(self.text_preview)\n                \n   \
      \             self.top_block.top_grid_layout.addWidget(self.gui_container, 0,\
      \ 0, 1, 2)\n                \n                self.gui_timer = QTimer()\n  \
      \              self.gui_timer.setInterval(150)\n                self.gui_timer.timeout.connect(self.update_gui)\n\
      \                self.gui_timer.start()\n                print(\"[RX File] GUI\
      \ successfully initialized.\")\n            except Exception as e:\n       \
      \         print(f\"[RX File] GUI setup warning: {e}\")\n\n    def symbols_to_bytes(self,\
      \ syms):\n        n_bytes = len(syms) // 4\n        byte_arr = bytearray(n_bytes)\n\
      \        for i in range(n_bytes):\n            s0 = int(syms[4*i])\n       \
      \     s1 = int(syms[4*i + 1])\n            s2 = int(syms[4*i + 2])\n       \
      \     s3 = int(syms[4*i + 3])\n            byte_arr[i] = (s0 << 6) | (s1 <<\
      \ 4) | (s2 << 2) | s3\n        return bytes(byte_arr)\n\n    def update_gui(self):\n\
      \        if not self.status_label:\n            return\n            \n     \
      \   n_rcvd = len(self.received_chunks)\n        tot = self.total_chunks\n  \
      \      pct = int((n_rcvd / tot) * 100) if tot > 0 else 0\n        \n       \
      \ if self.file_name:\n            self.status_label.setText(\n             \
      \   f\"Receiving '{self.file_name}' ({self.file_size:,} B) | Chunks: {n_rcvd}/{tot}\
      \ ({pct}%) | CRC Errors: {self.crc_errors}\"\n            )\n        else:\n\
      \            self.status_label.setText(\n                f\"Scanning for File\
      \ Broadcast... | Packets: {self.total_packets:,} | CRC Errors: {self.crc_errors}\"\
      \n            )\n            \n        if self.progress_bar:\n            self.progress_bar.setValue(pct)\n\
      \            if self.is_completed:\n                self.progress_bar.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                    \"QProgressBar { background-color: #313244; color: #11111b;\
      \ border-radius: 4px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; height: 22px; }\
      \ \"\n                    \"QProgressBar::chunk { background-color: #a6e3a1;\
      \ border-radius: 4px; }\"\n                )\n                \n        if self.is_completed\
      \ and self.result_label:\n            self.result_label.setText(\n         \
      \       f\"FILE SAVED: {self.saved_file_path}  |  CRC32: {hex(self.expected_crc)}\
      \ [VERIFIED 100%]\"\n            )\n            self.result_label.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                \"background-color: #1e3a24; color: #a6e3a1; font-size: 12px;\
      \ font-weight: bold; padding: 4px; border-radius: 4px;\"\n            )\n  \
      \          if self.text_preview and self.text_preview.toPlainText() == \"\"\
      :\n                self.text_preview.setPlainText(self.last_preview_text)\n\n\
      \    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n        in_syms = input_items[0]\n\
      \        if len(in_syms) == 0:\n            return 0\n            \n       \
      \ data = np.concatenate([self.buffer, in_syms])\n        idx = 0\n        n_data\
      \ = len(data)\n        \n        # Preamble (32) + Header (10 bytes = 40 syms)\
      \ = 72 symbols min\n        while idx + 72 <= n_data:\n            window =\
      \ data[idx : idx + 32]\n            mismatches = int(np.sum(window != self.preamble))\n\
      \            \n            if mismatches <= 2:\n                # Descramble\
      \ 10 header bytes\n                hdr_raw = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx\
      \ + 32 : idx + 72]))\n                for i in range(10):\n                \
      \    hdr_raw[i] ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[i % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n            \
      \        \n                magic, pkt_type, file_id, chunk_id, total_chunks,\
      \ payload_len = struct.unpack('>H B B H H H', bytes(hdr_raw))\n            \
      \    \n                if magic != 0x5AA5 or payload_len > 512:\n          \
      \          idx += 1\n                    continue\n                    \n  \
      \              total_pkt_syms = 32 + 40 + (4 * payload_len) + 16\n         \
      \       if idx + total_pkt_syms > n_data:\n                    break\n     \
      \               \n                # Descramble payload\n                pay_raw\
      \ = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx + 72 : idx + 72 + 4 * payload_len]))\n\
      \                for j in range(len(pay_raw)):\n                    pay_raw[j]\
      \ ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[(10 + j) % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n                   \
      \ \n                # Descramble CRC\n                crc_raw = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx\
      \ + 72 + 4 * payload_len : idx + total_pkt_syms]))\n                for k in\
      \ range(4):\n                    crc_raw[k] ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[(10 + payload_len\
      \ + k) % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n                    \n                r_crc =\
      \ struct.unpack('>I', bytes(crc_raw))[0]\n                calc_crc = zlib.crc32(bytes(hdr_raw)\
      \ + bytes(pay_raw)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n                \n                if calc_crc\
      \ == r_crc:\n                    self.total_packets += 1\n                 \
      \   \n                    # 1. Metadata Packet\n                    if pkt_type\
      \ == 0x10 and len(pay_raw) >= 8:\n                        r_size, r_fcrc = struct.unpack('>I\
      \ I', bytes(pay_raw[:8]))\n                        r_name = bytes(pay_raw[8:]).decode('utf-8',\
      \ errors='replace')\n                        \n                        if self.current_file_id\
      \ != file_id or self.file_name != r_name:\n                            print(f\"\
      \\n[RX File] New Broadcast Detected: '{r_name}' ({r_size} B, {total_chunks}\
      \ chunks)\")\n                            self.current_file_id = file_id\n \
      \                           self.file_name = r_name\n                      \
      \      self.file_size = r_size\n                            self.expected_crc\
      \ = r_fcrc\n                            self.total_chunks = total_chunks\n \
      \                           self.received_chunks = {}\n                    \
      \        self.is_completed = False\n                            \n         \
      \           # 2. Data Packet\n                    elif pkt_type == 0x11:\n \
      \                       if self.current_file_id == file_id:\n              \
      \              if chunk_id not in self.received_chunks:\n                  \
      \              self.received_chunks[chunk_id] = bytes(pay_raw)\n           \
      \                     if len(self.received_chunks) % 5 == 0 or len(self.received_chunks)\
      \ == total_chunks:\n                                    print(f\"[RX File] Chunk\
      \ {chunk_id + 1}/{total_chunks} (Total: {len(self.received_chunks)}/{total_chunks})\"\
      )\n                                    \n                            # Check\
      \ for completion\n                            if not self.is_completed and len(self.received_chunks)\
      \ == self.total_chunks and self.total_chunks > 0:\n                        \
      \        full_file = b\"\".join([self.received_chunks[i] for i in range(self.total_chunks)])\n\
      \                                calc_fcrc = zlib.crc32(full_file) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\
      \                                if calc_fcrc == self.expected_crc:\n      \
      \                              self.is_completed = True\n                  \
      \                  save_dir = self.save_dir\n                              \
      \      if not os.path.isabs(save_dir):\n                                   \
      \     d_path = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)) if '__file__' in locals()\
      \ else '.'\n                                        save_dir = os.path.join(d_path,\
      \ save_dir)\n                                        \n                    \
      \                out_name = \"received_\" + self.file_name\n               \
      \                     self.saved_file_path = os.path.join(save_dir, out_name)\n\
      \                                    try:\n                                \
      \        with open(self.saved_file_path, 'wb') as f:\n                     \
      \                       f.write(full_file)\n                               \
      \         print(f\"\\n========================================================\"\
      )\n                                        print(f\"*** FILE RECONSTRUCTION\
      \ 100% COMPLETE! ***\")\n                                        print(f\"File\
      \ Saved: {self.saved_file_path}\")\n                                       \
      \ print(f\"File Size: {len(full_file):,} Bytes\")\n                        \
      \                print(f\"CRC32 Check: {hex(calc_fcrc)} (PASS)\")\n        \
      \                                print(f\"========================================================\\\
      n\")\n                                        self.last_preview_text = full_file.decode('utf-8',\
      \ errors='replace')[:4000]\n                                    except Exception\
      \ as e:\n                                        print(f\"[RX File] File save\
      \ error: {e}\")\n                                else:\n                   \
      \                 print(f\"[RX File WARNING] File CRC mismatch! Expected {hex(self.expected_crc)},\
      \ got {hex(calc_fcrc)}\")\n                    idx += total_pkt_syms\n     \
      \           else:\n                    self.crc_errors += 1\n              \
      \      idx += total_pkt_syms\n            else:\n                idx += 1\n\
      \                \n        if idx < n_data:\n            self.buffer = data[idx:]\n\
      \        else:\n            self.buffer = np.array([], dtype=np.uint8)\n   \
      \         \n        if len(self.buffer) > 10000:\n            self.buffer =\
      \ self.buffer[-2000:]\n            \n        return len(in_syms)\n\n    def\
      \ stop(self):\n        if hasattr(self, 'gui_timer') and self.gui_timer:\n \
      \           self.gui_timer.stop()\n        return True\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: QPSK File Deframer, CRC32 Check & GUI Progress
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    save_dir: '''.'''
  states:
    _io_cache: ('File Deframer & GUI', 'blk', [('save_dir', "'.'")], [('0', 'byte',
      1)], [], 'Robust QPSK File Deframer, CRC32 Verifier & In-Window GUI Progress
      Display', ['save_dir'])
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 1392
    - 320.0
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_0
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: "======================================================================\n\
      \           QPSK RECEIVER SYNCHRONIZATION TUNING GUIDE\n======================================================================\n\
      \n1. COSTAS LOOP BANDWIDTH (costas_loop_bw):\n   - What it does:\n     Tracks\
      \ carrier phase and eliminates fine carrier frequency offset\n     between the\
      \ transmitter and receiver oscillators.\n   - How to adjust:\n     * HIGHER\
      \ (0.06 - 0.10):\n       Widens the frequency acquisition (pull-in) range. Crucial\
      \ when\n       operating at high RF frequencies (e.g., 2.85 GHz) where USRP\
      \ TCXO\n       crystal offsets are 5 kHz - 12 kHz.\n       * Symptom if too\
      \ low (< 0.04): Constellation fails to lock and\n         spins in 8 clusters\
      \ (dynamic phase slips across 45-deg boundaries).\n       * Symptom if too high\
      \ (> 0.15): Constellation clusters smear/blur\n         due to excessive phase\
      \ noise tracking.\n     * Recommendation:\n       Keep default at 0.07 - 0.08\
      \ for instant hardware capture.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\
      \n2. TIMING LOOP BANDWIDTH (timing_loop_bw):\n   - What it does:\n     Symbol\
      \ clock synchronization (Gardner TED in Symbol Sync block).\n     Finds the\
      \ exact optimal time instant to sample each symbol at 1 SPS.\n   - How to adjust:\n\
      \     * HIGHER (0.02 - 0.05):\n       Faster clock lock; tracks sudden sample-rate\
      \ clock drift.\n     * LOWER (0.005 - 0.015):\n       Minimizes timing jitter\
      \ and inter-symbol interference (ISI).\n     * Recommendation:\n       Keep\
      \ at 0.01. Only increase if constellation points spread radially\n       along\
      \ symbol transition trajectories.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\
      \n3. FLL BAND-EDGE BANDWIDTH (w in digital_fll_band_edge_cc):\n   - What it\
      \ does:\n     Performs coarse carrier frequency offset estimation by balancing\n\
      \     energy at the upper and lower Nyquist band edges (+/- (1+Alpha)*Rs/2).\n\
      \   - How to adjust:\n     * Set to 0.03 - 0.05 to rapidly pull in large initial\
      \ crystal offsets\n       before the signal reaches the Costas loop.\n     *\
      \ If set too low (0.01), convergence is sluggish, forcing the Costas\n     \
      \  loop to do all the heavy lifting.\n======================================================================"
    note: receiver tuning guide
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 544
    - 512.0
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
